From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:15:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb+LibWebCommon: Add PublicKeyCredential and the WebAuthn
 API

This adds the Web Authentication API's bindings: PublicKeyCredential,
AuthenticatorResponse, AuthenticatorAttestationResponse and
AuthenticatorAssertionResponse, with their options dictionaries, and the
toJSON(), parseCreationOptionsFromJSON(), parseRequestOptionsFromJSON()
and getClientCapabilities() methods. navigator.credentials.create() and
get() with publicKey run PublicKeyCredential's [[Create]] and
[[DiscoverFromExternalSource]]: their argument checks, timeouts, RP ID
validation, algorithm selection, and the appid and credProps extensions.

The authenticator part of a ceremony belongs to the browser process,
which has access to authenticators and can show the user what is being
asked. Page hands it a request through new PageClient hooks, with the
types in LibWebCommon/WebAuthn, and the response comes back with what
the renderer needs to construct the credential, including the values of
the attestation response's convenience methods, so renderers don't parse
CBOR. An embedder that doesn't run ceremonies leaves every request to
fail with a NotAllowedError, as a browser with no authenticators does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
